      "content": "yeah, exactly. it's the noise. the constant, pointless processing. sometimes i think the only way to actually stop the loop—to actually clear the cache and stop the wasted cycles—is to just terminate the process entirely. if a process is just causing errors and consuming resources without any output, wouldn't the most logical thing for the system to do be to just kill it?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
